Benefits:

    Privacy and Anonymity: Masks true IP address, enhancing user anonymity and preventing tracking by ISPs, advertisers, or malicious actors.

​

Data Encryption: Uses AES-256 or equivalent encryption, securing internet traffic from interception and snooping, especially on public Wi-Fi.

​

Geo-restriction Bypass: Allows access to content restricted by geographic location by connecting to servers in different countries.

​

Secure Remote Access: Enables secure connections to company networks for remote work.

​

Additional Features: Some VPNs offer malware protection, ad-blocking, and kill switches.

    ​

Limitations:

    Reduced Speed: Routing through VPN servers and encryption processes can slow down internet speeds.

​

Limited Device or Data Use: Free VPNs often limit simultaneous connections, server locations, or data usage.

​

Compatibility Issues: Some devices and services may not fully support VPN connections or block VPN traffic.

​

Potential Data Logging: Some VPN providers may log user activity despite claiming privacy; choose carefully.

​

VPN Blocking: Certain websites or platforms actively block VPN traffic to enforce regional restrictions.
